    'The Serengeti National Park is Tanzania\'s most celebrated park and one of the oldest and most studied ecosystems in the world. The name comes from the Maasai "Siringitu" meaning "endless plains," and the description holds — 14,750 km² of open grassland, acacia woodland and river ecosystems that stretch to the horizon in every direction.',
    'The park is the southern portion of the greater Serengeti-Mara ecosystem, which extends north into Kenya\'s Masai Mara. Together they host the Great Migration — the year-round circular movement of over 1.5 million wildebeest, 200,000 zebras and 300,000 Thomson\'s gazelles. The migration passes through different sections of the Serengeti in different months, making the park rewarding for wildlife viewing every month of the year.',
