      'January to February: Calving season on the short grass plains of the southern Serengeti and Ngorongoro Conservation Area. Approximately 500,000 calves are born in a 3-week window. Exceptional predator concentrations. Underrated and far less crowded than peak season.',
      'March to May: Herds on the move north through the central Serengeti as the long rains begin. Some camps close. Dramatic green landscapes and excellent birding.',
