const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is the Serengeti good for wildlife outside migration season?', a: 'Yes. The Serengeti has outstanding wildlife year-round. The resident population of lions, leopards, cheetahs, elephants, buffaloes, zebras and Thomson\'s gazelles is enormous regardless of whether the migrating herds are present. January and February\'s calving season is arguably the most dramatic wildlife event in the Serengeti calendar.' },
  { q: 'How many nights should I spend in the Serengeti?', a: 'A minimum of 2 nights allows two full days of game drives. Three to four nights is much better and allows you to explore different zones — central Seronera, northern Kogatende (for river crossings) or southern short grass plains (for calving). More nights means more chances of seeing elusive species like leopard and wild dog.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between Serengeti camp types?', a: 'The Serengeti has three main camp tiers. Permanent tented camps and lodges offer year-round comfortable accommodation in fixed locations. Mobile camps move seasonally to follow the migration. Budget camping is available at public campsites near Seronera. We recommend permanent tented camps for the best balance of comfort, guiding quality and location.' },
